# Source renders — 293 MB and 592 MB, and only ever inputs to `npm run frames`.
# The optimised WebP the site actually serves is committed under public/frames,
# so a fresh clone builds and deploys without them.
#
#   DESKTOP FRAMES/  the 16:9 landscape render, 1280x720
#   Mobile/          the 9:16 portrait render, 1080x1920
#
# Anchored with a leading slash so they match only these two folders at the
# repository root. Unanchored, "Mobile/" matches a directory of that name at
# any depth — and git is case-insensitive here — so it also swallowed the
# generated public/stills/mobile/ and public/frames/mobile/.
/DESKTOP FRAMES/
/Mobile/
